content.text:
Now LocationView layout/touch. This is the biggest.

Changes:
- constants: BAG_Y -320, HOLD_UI_Y -505, FLOOR_Y -60, box container y 330.
- show: add hint label; buttons use alignBottom; box layout.
- box layout: 3 cols, spacing adaptive; compute base position helper for render and updateHold.
- floor slot: safe width, wrap; hint.
- drag rewrite coordinates; attach touch in spawnItemToFloor.
- menu: "放入背包" + Chinese, size.
- time? not here.

Let's define helpers:
```
private boxCols(): number { return 3; }
private boxSpacing(): {x:number,y:number} {
  const safeW = Math.min(720, UILayout.visibleW) - 40;
  const x = Math.min(180, (safeW - BIG_BOX) / 2);
  return { x: Math.max(120, x), y: 168 };
}
private getBoxBasePosition(index:number,total:number): Vec3 {
  const cols=3;
  const row=Math.floor(index/cols);
  const col=index%cols;
  const inRow=Math.min(cols, total-row*cols);
  const sp=this.boxSpacing();
  return new Vec3((col-(inRow-1)/2)*sp.x, -row*sp.y, 0);
}
```
For 3 boxes: row0 inRow3 → -sp,0,sp. For 4: row0 3, row1 1 center. Good.
For safeW 592-40=552; (552-144)/2=204 → min 180. spacing 180; edges 180+72=252 < 296. Good.
For 6: rows 3+3, y 0,-168. Box container y=330 → rows 330,162; box half 72 → 402 top < 470 HUD bottom. Floor at -60, top 50; row2 bottom 162-72=90, gap. Good.

Update `renderBoxes` and `updateHold` to use helper (no more col/spacing duplicated).

Floor slots: 
```
private getFloorSlotPosition(index:number): Vec3 {
 const n=Math.max(1,this.game.floor.length);
 const perRow=6;
 const row=Math.floor(index/perRow);
 const col=index%perRow;
 const inRow=Math.min(perRow, n-row*perRow);
 const safeW=Math.min(720,UILayout.visibleW)-48;
 const spacing=Math.min(70, (safeW-56)/Math.max(1,inRow-1));
 return new Vec3((col-(inRow-1)/2)*Math.max(44,spacing), 40-row*70, 0);
}
```
Floor container y=-60, so items y around -20 and -90; bag top -160 (BAG_Y -320 + 160). Floor height 220; fine.
For 1 item spacing denominator 1 → (safeW-56) huge → min 70. centered.

Hint label in show:
```
const hint = this.createTextLabel? Use uiNode + UITransform + Label.
```
Add a helper `makeLabel(text,size,color,pos,w,h)` in LocationView. Or inline.
Hint at (0, -535) text "拖动或单击物品放入背包" font 20 color gray. Ensure not overlapping buttons (bottom -? button center -592, top -564); hint -535 okay. With safeBottom, buttons move up to -558, top -530; hint -535 overlaps. Put hint at -505? Hold UI at -505. Hmm. Put hint at y=-500 and hold UI at -470? Bag bottom -480. Let's compute:
- Bag 4x4 spans -160..-480.
- holdUI at -505 (height 100, labels at -525) might overlap buttons when safeBottom 34 (buttons center -558, top -530). Hold UI label at -525, okay close.
- hint at -548? overlaps.
Maybe remove hint on location page and rely on text in hold UI? The requirement doesn't require hint. But a hint helps. Put hint at top of floor: y=10? Floor items at -20. 
Place hint at y=-125 (between floor and bag top -160): "拖动 / 单击物品放入背包" font 18. Floor container -60, floor items rows at -20,-90; bag top -160. y=-130 is free. Use hint at y=-132. Good.

Buttons: leave/home at x ±180, y=0 then alignBottom(btn, 24). On 390 device, x ±180 +70=250 <296. Good.
- `leaveBtn` calls leaveLocation then onLeave; okay.
- home button Fx text `回家需 ¥${cost}` should be 体力 not ¥. Fix to "回家消耗 X 体力" (not requirement but bug).
- Add a "背包" label? no.

Spawning items: attach touch.
```
private attachFloorTouch(node,uid) { ... }
```
Already defined; call after adding in spawnItemToFloor before animation. But node parent changes after; listeners persist.

Drag rewrite:

Fields: `dragOffset` view-space; `touchStartPos` view-space; `touchStartTime`.

```
private onFloorTouchStart(event, uid) {
  if (this.draggingUid !== null || this.holdBoxId) return;
  const node=...; if(!node||!viewNode) return;
  this.potentialDrag=true; this.isDragging=false;
  this.touchStartPos=this.getTouchLocal(event,this.viewNode);
  this.touchStartTime=Date.now();
  this.draggingUid=uid; this.draggingNode=node;
  const nodeView=this.viewNode.getComponent(UITransform)!.convertToNodeSpaceAR(node.getWorldPosition());
  this.dragOffset=new Vec3(nodeView.x-this.touchStartPos.x,nodeView.y-this.touchStartPos.y,0);
}
```
`onFloorTouchMove`:
```
if (draggingUid!==uid||!potentialDrag||!viewNode||!draggingNode) return;
const touchView=this.getTouchLocal(event,this.viewNode);
if(!this.isDragging && Vec3.distance(touchStartPos,touchView)>16) {
  this.isDragging=true; this.potentialDrag=false;
  const world=this.draggingNode.getWorldPosition();
  const local=viewUt.convertToNodeSpaceAR(world);
  this.draggingNode.setParent(this.viewNode);
