Hint text is light gray, low contrast on dark background. "颜色加深" likely means make it darker/more visible? Chinese "颜色加深" = deepen the color (darker). But on a dark background, darker would be less visible; maybe they mean deepen (more saturated/darker) from washed-out white. Screenshot hint is gray on dark, hard to read. A dark text with light stroke/background would help. Could add a semi-opaque dark/cream background pill behind the hint, and set text color deep brown/black? The requirement specifically "提示字颜色加深" — change color to a darker color. Since the background is dark, maybe use a bright cream? Hmm.

Maybe the hint appears over a bright area in their test; they want darker. We can set text to `new Color(35, 30, 25, 255)` (deep brown/black) and add a light semi-transparent background strip behind it so it stays readable on dark. But adding background changes look; okay. Or set `new Color(60, 40, 20, 235)` plus a cream outline? Cocos Label supports outline via `LabelOutline` component. Could add `LabelOutline` with color white and width 2, and dark fill; then readable on both. That meets "颜色加深" while keeping contrast.

Let's use `LabelOutline` from cc:
```
import { LabelOutline } from 'cc';
const outline = hint.addComponent(LabelOutline);
outline.color = new Color(255,255,255,200);
outline.width = 2;
lb.color = new Color(45,35,25,255);
```
But LabelOutline type exists. tsc. This gives dark text with light outline. Good.

Alternatively add a semi-transparent background: create a Graphics rect behind hint with cream alpha 180, dark text. That would be more visible. But "颜色加深" likely just text. Use outline + dark.

Now top-right amount blocked by capsule. View r2 screenshot r2_20_d1_fortune shows money at top-right ¥0.00, capsule not visible in screenshot (web test). In WeChat the capsule overlays it. Implement capsule inset.

Need ensure `UILayout` queries wx. `wx` type available? `types/wx.d.ts` in cocos; GameRoot uses `(globalThis as any).wx` elsewhere. Use any.

