```
static capsuleBottom = 0;
static capsuleLeft = 0;
...
try {
 const wxAny:any=(globalThis as any).wx;
 if (wxAny && typeof wxAny.getMenuButtonBoundingClientRect==='function') {
   const rect=wxAny.getMenuButtonBoundingClientRect();
   if (rect && rect.bottom>0 && frameH>0) {
     const scale = 1280/frameH;
     this.capsuleBottom = Math.max(0, rect.bottom*scale);
     this.capsuleLeft = Math.max(0, rect.left*scale);
   }
 }
} catch {}
```
But `rect.bottom` is pixels from top of screen. Design H=1280, scale=1280/frameH. On 390x844: 58*1.516=88.
`capsuleLeft` design x from left: rect.left*scale. Not needed if moving down.

`headerTop = Math.max(safeTop, capsuleBottom)`.
Add getter:
```
static get headerTop(){ return Math.max(this.safeTop, this.capsuleBottom); }
```
Change `alignTop` and `alignTopSide` to use `headerTop` instead of `safeTop`.
HUD strip use `headerTop`.
`buildHUD` topY = UILayout.top - (headerTop - safeTop)? Wait `UILayout.top = visibleH/2 - safeTop`. The design top edge is `visibleH/2=640`. Header top margin from top = headerTop. So label y should be `640 - headerTop - 20` (center). `UILayout.top` = 640 - safeTop. If capsuleBottom>safeTop, we need `top - (headerTop-safeTop) - 20`. Define `UILayout.headerY = visibleH/2 - headerTop` (the y-coordinate of header top). Then topY = headerY - 24. Bars headerY - 62. Home cost headerY - 94.
Currently buildHUD uses `UILayout.top - 24` etc. Replace with `UILayout.headerY`.
Strip position y = headerY - hudH/2, height hudH = headerTop + 118. Actually strip top at visibleH/2 (screen top), bottom at headerY - 118. Height = headerTop+118, center = (visibleH/2 + (headerY-118))/2 = visibleH/2 - (headerTop+118)/2. Set size (visibleW+40, headerTop+118), position y = visibleH/2 - (headerTop+118)/2. Or simply strip top at 640, height headerTop+118. Good.
`alignTop` widget top = headerTop + margin. `headerY` = 640 - headerTop.
`alignTopSide` same.

