content.text:
Now add tests for event resolution and report. Let's edit test/game.test.ts. Find end and add. Need imports already include Game, CONFIG, ITEMS, LOCATIONS. PendingEvent type? We can use any.

Test event resolution:
```
test('所有事件 resolveEvent 后离开 event 状态', () => {
  const cases = [
    {id:'patrol', opt:0, win:false},
    {id:'patrol', opt:1, win:false},
    {id:'guard', opt:0, win:false},
    {id:'rival', opt:0, win:false},
    {id:'rival', opt:1, win:true},
    {id:'rival', opt:1, win:false},
    {id:'auntie', opt:0, win:false},
    {id:'delivery', opt:0, win:false},
    {id:'wallet', opt:0, win:false},
    {id:'cat', opt:0, win:false},
    {id:'rain', opt:0, win:false},
  ];
  for (const c of cases) {
    const g = newGame();
    g.day = 5; g.phase='event'; g.location='baishizhou'; g.stamina=50; g.hunger=50; g.money=0;
    (g as any).pendingEvent = {id:c.id, name:c.id, options:[]};
    g.resolveEvent(c.opt, c.win);
    assert.notEqual(g.phase,'event', `${c.id}/${c.opt}`);
    assert.equal((g as any).pendingEvent, null, `${c.id}`);
  }
});
```
But `newGame()` starts with day1, fortune; setting phase event, location. For `rival` option 1 win true adds box; phase location. For `rival` lose stamina 10; 50→40. For `patrol` option1 uses rng chance; phase location or map. For `cat` option0 `findEdibleUid` none; phase location. For `rain`, phase location. Good.
- `hunger=50`, dailyHunger at day5 is 38; no death.
- `money=0` for wallet; adds 20.
- `pendingEvent` typed any.

Need `g.resolveEvent` requires `this.pendingEvent` non-null; yes.

Test report:
```
test('日结算最离谱与今日战绩同一件物品，金额不拆行', () => {
  const g=newGame(); g.phase='location'; g.location='baishizhou'; g.stamina=50;
  g.bag=[
   {uid:1,itemId:'old_newspaper',x:0,y:0,w:1,h:1},
   {uid:2,itemId:'old_phone',x:1,y:0,w:1,h:1},
  ];
  assert.equal(g.goHome(),true);
  const r=g.lastDayReport!;
  assert.equal(r.bestItem,'旧手机');
  assert.ok(r.quip.includes('旧手机'));
  assert.ok(r.quip.includes('¥\u00A0'));
  assert.ok(!/¥\s/.test(r.quip.replace('¥\u00A0',''))); // maybe not needed
});
```
The regex `¥\s` with NBSP: JS \s matches NBSP, so bad. Just assert includes NBSP and not includes `'¥ '` regular space. `assert.ok(!r.quip.includes('¥ '))`.
- `bestItem` expected old_phone price 54 vs newspaper 0.5. Yes.
- `goHome` requires `stamina >= homeCost` (5); 50.
- `phase` location, location baishizhou.
- After goHome, phase home, report.
- `income` 54.5.

But note `makeDayQuip` uses `\u00A0`; `r.quip` includes actual NBSP. JS string `'¥\u00A0'` okay.

Add tests at end.

