block.text:
Now item icons restructure.

Need know rarity glow names and colors. Define constants:
```
const FLOOR_ICON = 48;
const FLOOR_PLATE = 56;
const FLOOR_GLOW = 64;
const BAG_ICON = 32;
const BAG_PLATE = 40;
```
Remove `ITEM_SIZE`, `ITEM_PLATE` or rename. Current code uses `ITEM_SIZE`/`ITEM_PLATE` only in createItemNode. We'll replace.

`createItemNode(item, def, color, context: 'floor'|'bag' = 'floor')`:
```
const isFloor = context==='floor';
const iconSize = isFloor?48:32;
const plateSize = isFloor?56:40;
const root = uiNode('item_'+id);
const rut=...setContentSize(plateSize,plateSize); anchor .5;
const hit=root.addComponent(Graphics); hit.fillColor = new Color(0,0,0,0); hit.rect(-plateSize/2,...); hit.fill(); // maybe alpha 0
if (isFloor) {
  const glow = this.createRarityGlow(def?.rarity ?? 'common', FLOOR_GLOW);
  glow.parent=root; glow.setPosition(0,0,0);
}
const plate=uiNode('plate'); parent root; UT plateSize; const pg=Graphics; fill Color(0,0,0,140); roundRect; fill; maybe stroke;
const icon=Art.makeVisual(..., iconSize, iconSize, fallbackColor, def?.name...); parent root; pos 0; anchor .5;
const outline=uiNode('outline'); parent root; UT iconSize; Graphics strokeColor (0,0,0,220); lineWidth 1; rect(-iconSize/2+0.5...); stroke;
return root;
```
- Root hit Graphics transparent; but adding multiple Graphics components? Only one root; plate/outline children each own. Fine.
- If root transparent Graphics with alpha 0, does it count for renderer/hit? UITransform is there; okay. Could set alpha 1 to be safe but invisible. Use `new Color(0,0,0,1)` nearly invisible. It may tint 1/255 negligible. Use 1.
- Plate #000 alpha 0.55: 140/255=0.549. Use 140.
- Glow ring: `createRarityGlow`:
```
private glowForRarity(rarity: Rarity): {name:string; color:Color} {
 switch: common white (255,255,255), good blue (90,180,255), rare gold (255,210,80), epic rainbow (255,120,255), mishap white/red (255,120,120)
}
const glow=Art.makeVisual(name, FLOOR_GLOW, FLOOR_GLOW, color);
glow.parent=root;
const sp=glow.getComponent(Sprite); if(sp) sp.color=color;
// if no frames, placeholder is a solid block; to keep ring, maybe plate covers center; okay.
```
- The glow sprite frame is 48x48; displayed 64 (non-integer 1.333x). Requirement "reuse fx/glow_* sprites"; integer scaling? It says loot icons 3x integer; glow ring can be 64 maybe. Could use 48x48 glow (1x) or 96 (2x). Outer ring around plate 56: use 64 (non-integer) would blur? Nearest filtering; but integer requirement only icons. To be pixel-perfect, use 72? 48*1.5 not integer. Use 96 (2x) outer ring; bigger, may overlap adjacent floor items spacing 84. Glow 96 > 84, overlaps neighbors; but glow transparent. Could use 48 (1x) ring, smaller than plate 56, hidden. Use 64; acceptable. Or 72 (1.5x). Requirement doesn't specify glow size. Use 64.
- `Art.makeVisual` for glow with frames; `applySpriteToNode` sets size 64; Sprite tint via `sp.color`. Does `Sprite.color` work? yes. Could set `UIOpacity` 200 for subtle. Add.
- Outline: draw rect around icon exactly; if icon is 48, lineWidth 1; `g.rect(-24,-24,48,48)`. But if icon sprite has transparent padding, outline at node bounds; okay.
- For bag icons, no glow, plate 40, icon 32, outline 32.
- Floor spacing currently 84; plate 56, glow 64; okay.
- Bag root 40; `placeBagNode` uses root size 40; icon 32; good.
- `placeBagNode` anchor correction: root 40 anchor .5; center.
- Floor positions root 56; spacing 84; okay.
- Hint at 42; floor row0 local 50, root 56 top 78 (world 18); hint 42 (32..52) may overlap floor icon top 18? No, hint bottom 32 > icon top 18? Wait floor container -60, row0 local 50 → world -10; root half28 top 18. Hint y42 spans 32..52; gap 14. Good. Box bottom 90; hint top52; gap. Fine.
- Two rows: row1 local -34 → world -94, half28 bottom -122; bag top -140; hint unaffected.

- `createItemNode` calls:
  - `spawnItemToFloor`: pass 'floor'.
  - `renderFloor`: 'floor'.
  - `renderBag`: 'bag'.
- For floor item drag, root 56; hit area 56; okay.
- For item menu, title; okay.

- `clearBagView`; root children destroy.

Let's implement.

